{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"b1","type":"objection","text":"The account diagnoses the recurring meaning-disputes as innocent shared-memory failure and builds the remedy on that, yet a1's own hedge concedes bad faith is not excluded. If a flatmate benefits from interpretive slack, they will resist or game the written trial itself, and the account's only failure contingency is the avoiding friend's refusal, with the viability of the living arrangement as the sole fallback.","target":["h005.fork5.p.objection.0#a1","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#a4"],"grounds":"The material does not distinguish sincere memory divergence from strategic ambiguity; the remedy assumes the former.","bearing":"Limits the claimed sufficiency of the written-agreement trial; identifies a missing mid-level contingency."},{"id":"b2","type":"objection","text":"Counting asynchronous edits as full participation conflates participation in the conversation with contribution to household labor. Under a disengagement reading of the avoidance, the channel certifies minimal engagement as full participation. The account reads refusal of the channel as diagnostic but does not read acceptance as diagnostic, and a5 requires no link between written input and observable chore outcomes.","target":["h005.fork5.p.objection.0#a5","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#a3"],"grounds":"a3 is avowedly a conjecture; alternative readings of avoidance make acceptance as ambiguous as refusal.","bearing":"The consequence claimed for a5 is unsupported unless participation is redefined or paired with outcome checks."},{"id":"b3","type":"objection","text":"The remedy stack optimizes coordination while never considering options that shrink the coordination surface — domain ownership or paying for cleaning — and never weighs the cost of bureaucratizing a friendship. By the account's own churn claim, decoupled arrangements degrade gracefully while negotiated weekly resets degrade badly.","target":["h005.fork5.p.objection.0#a4","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#a5","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#a6"],"grounds":"Changing schedules (a2) undermine time-keyed coordination; the material does not show stakes large enough to justify the overhead either way.","bearing":"Challenges the strategy family represented by the account's uptake rather than any single step; proportionality is unresolved."},{"id":"b4","type":"objection","text":"The two-week trial has no pre-agreed success criterion. A household prone to retroactive disagreement about what agreements meant will predictably disagree about whether the trial worked, reproducing the diagnosed failure one level up.","target":["h005.fork5.p.objection.0#a4"],"bearing":"Bounded: fixable by recording a verdict test with the trial, but under schedule churn that test is itself contestable, so the fix is substantive."},{"id":"b5","type":"objection","text":"Done-criteria presuppose agreement on standards. If some disputes concern what counts as clean rather than what was agreed, drafting criteria relocates the argument to drafting time rather than resolving it, and fewer disputes will be checkable against the record than the trial's promised consequence suggests.","target":["h005.fork5.p.objection.0#a1","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#a4"],"bearing":"Narrows the class of disputes a4's consequence covers; does not defeat the trial, since surfacing standards conflict could still count as progress."},{"id":"b6","type":"problem","text":"Unresolved: whether the disagreements about past agreements are sincere on all sides, and what the asker should do if the written trial is refused or gamed by someone who keeps attending every conversation — a contingency between 'the trial works' and 'the living arrangement is unviable' that neither the account nor this objection resolves."},{"id":"b7","type":"use","text":"If the account's proposals are taken up, prefix the trial with an explicit, recorded success criterion and attach a pre-named fallback branch — decoupled chore domains or a paid-cleaning option — for the case where the trial is refused, gamed, or judges itself a failure.","target":["h005.fork5.p.objection.0#a4","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#a5"],"depends":["b1","b3","b4"]}],"uptake":["b1","b2","b3","b4","b5","b7"]}